/NM (4aa3f251\0551e4a\0554411\05583ff\05519fe795047ec)
/Rect [ 66.812 52.174684 566.598 565.894 ]
/T (Text Field50)
/V (On 08Oct26 \050Day 14 read\051\054 initial test results were recorded as Inconclusive due to formulation\055induced turbidity inherent to the concentrated Sermorelin sample matrix\056 In accordance with USP \07471\076 and laboratory procedure for turbid samples\054 aliquots were aseptically subcultured into fresh media bottles on 07Oct26 by analyst Ayomide Odugbesi and returned to incubation\056\012\012On 12Oct26 \050Day 18 of the original bottles and Day 5 of the subculture aliquots\051\054 microbial growth was observed and confirmed in both original TSB bottle and subcultured TSB bottle \1332 x 200mL TSB \050Original and Subculture Bottles\051\135 by reading analyst Andrew Carrillo and verified by laboratory supervisor\056 The FTM media bottles \050original and subculture\051 remained clear and negative \050No Growth\051 throughout the entire incubation period\056 Positive TSB bottles were submitted for Differential Staining and Microbial Identification under submission ETX\055261012\0550367\056 Differential staining indicated Gram\055positive rods\056 Definitive identification confirmed the isolate as Bacillus megaterium\054 as detailed in Table 1\056\012\012All culture media and consumables utilized were within their valid manufacturer expiration dates\056 Negative control media bottles for direct inoculation were manipulated and incubated alongside the test samples under identical conditions\073 both TSB and FTM negative controls demonstrated complete absence of microbial growth \050No Growth\051\054 verifying media sterility and aseptic technique\056\012\012Attached Table 2 details the environmental monitoring data associated with sample processing on 23Sep26\056 Environmental monitoring plates were incubated in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0552\054 Environmental Monitoring of the Clean\055room Facility\056 Review of contemporaneous personnel monitoring \050left\055 and right\055hand touch plates for analyst Guanchen Li\051 and ISO 5 BSC E001314 monitoring \050surface contact plates and settling plates\051 demonstrated No Growth across all sampling locations on the date of testing \05023Sep26\051\054 the date before testing \05022Sep26\051\054 and the date after testing \05024Sep26\051\056 These data confirm that processing personnel and the ISO 5 BSC were maintained in an optimal state of microbiological control and were not a source of contamination\056\012\012Routine weekly surface sampling of Cleanroom Suite 115 performed on 23Sep26 demonstrated No Growth\056 Weekly active\055air sampling of the outermost ISO 8 Room 115 recovered 6 CFUs \050ETX\055261001\0550625\051\056 Microbial identification confirmed these isolates as Micrococcus luteus \0504 CFUs\051\054 Kocuria indica and Kocuria rhizophila \0501 CFU\051\054 and one pending fungal isolate \050Pending FunITS\054 exhibiting hyphae morphology\054 1 CFU\051\056 Crucially\054 all recovered environmental isolates were Gram\055positive cocci or fungal hyphae\054 different from the Gram\055positive spore\055forming rod \050Bacillus megaterium\051 detected in the positive test sample\054 with zero Bacillus species recovered in the cleanroom environment\056 Furthermore\054 outermost Room 115 functions as an ISO 8 anteroom that is physically separated from innermost cleanroom 115B and the ISO 5 processing zone by cascaded airlocks and positive pressure differentials\056 The complete absence of microbial recovery across all critical ISO 7 rooms \050115A and 115B\051\054 personnel gloves\054 and ISO 5 BSC surfaces confirms that room air contaminants did not enter the ISO 5 critical work area\056\012\012Monthly cleaning and disinfection of the cleanrooms \050ISO 7\051 and their containing biosafety cabinets \050ISO 5\051 were performed on 13Sep26 for Suite 115\054 as per MICRO\055SOP\0559\054 Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\056 It was documented that all chemical indicators passed\054 which confirmed the efficient monthly cleaning of all cleanrooms in Suite 115\056\012\012Analyzing a 6\055month sample history for GoGoMeds Select \050E10747\051\054 this specific analyte \042Sermorelin 0\0569mg\057ml\042 has had no prior Out\055of\055Specification \050OOS\051 occurrences under USP \07471\076 sterility testing\056\012\012All samples processed on the same day were also evaluated for evidence of sample\055to\055sample cross\055contamination\056 During the original test setup on 23Sep26\054 the processing analyst handled another stability sample from the same client\054 ETX\055260624\0550206 \050T90\054 Sermorelin 3 mg\057mL\054 Lot 17008\051\054 which was processed under comparable conditions and yielded negative results for microbial growth\056 These findings confirm that sample\055to\055sample cross\055contamination is highly unlikely\056)
>>
endobj
